    {
      "name": "find_and_inspect",
      "description": "Search official sources, inspect a selected source compactly, page a selected dimension, or exactly look up schema value IDs or labels in one selected official dimension. Pass the context_id returned by plan_request. The model chooses every action, publisher, candidate, dimension, exact value, and cursor; large values stay paginated. Exact lookup checks schema membership only; it does not perform substring, synonym, translation, or concept matching. If a value is not known exactly, page the returned schema values and choose from them. Search uses lexical metadata/card matches and available source-card embeddings for candidate recall; embeddings do not select or validate a source. Review each bounded candidate card's official language, availability, access.queryable, dimension definitions, value samples, and generated source_card. A source card is a discovery hint with provenance, not official evidence or source authorization; confirm all semantic choices against the live inspected schema. This is discovery, not semantic source selection: choose the publisher from the plan and formulate a concise query using the candidate metadata's declared language. The Finnish Tax Administration has separate `vero` PxWeb and `vero-web` official decision-table providers. A nonempty candidate list does not mean it matches the plan. Do not use a candidate whose title/schema is for a related but different statistic; reformulate and search the same provider again. Start with one concise metadata term and limit 30; add a second term only to disambiguate. Search returns `candidate_tuple` field order `[candidate_id, title]`; inspect a returned candidate ID to see its dimensions. Search may be repeated at any later workflow stage to refine candidates. Then use only the returned source_ref for page, match, and retrieve. Inspection returns at most five value tuples per dimension by default; `value_tuple` declares their field order `[id, label, unit, definition]`. For several exact values in one dimension, send `value_texts` once (rather than separate match calls); `match_tuple` is `[text, values]`. Use `value_limit: 100` when all values of a large comparable dimension are needed, then continue with the returned cursor. Before retrieval, verify the inspected schema has the exact requested geography/entity and measure; if it does not, inspect another candidate. When no current candidate has the exact geography, reformulate the metadata query around the model-selected official statistic and geography level rather than retrieving a merely contextual source. Do not send blank optional fields or invent IDs. Follow workflow.allowed_next_actions.",
