    {
      "name": "answer_with_evidence",
      "description": "Pass the context_id returned by plan_request. Run server-side arithmetic, finalize evidence-linked answer claims, request clarification, or state that a request cannot be completed. For needs_clarification, provide structured clarification_questions; for cannot_complete, provide structured missing_scope. Use action=calculate for every derived numeric relationship (including differences, rates, shares, percentage changes, totals, or category counts); write one read-only SQL SELECT and use {{source}} exactly where the retrieved evidence relation belongs. Use only source.columns returned by a prior calculation response or the retrieved row headers. For action=finalize, submit assessments and claims after all required evidence/calculations are ready. The model decides which criteria are unmet from the retrieval plan and returned evidence; the assessment schema records coverage and source_availability gaps explicitly. If a request assessment has status proxy, every direct or derived claim for that request must be accompanied by a proxy_disclosure claim for the same request that cites the same evidence_id; describe the narrower measure or scope in the disclosure. A proxy_disclosure_required error returns the affected claim, request, and evidence IDs; repair it with those structured values without changing the assessment or bypassing other validation. Numeric claims not supported by each claim's cited rows, selected schema values, or linked calculation return claim_unsupported_numbers for correction; the current date is planning context, not evidence for an observation. If evidence is a narrower subtotal or the latest available period is older than requested, include its actual figure in an evidence-linked limitation claim, name its period, and state precisely what it excludes or why it is not the requested period; do not discard verified useful evidence. The model decides calculations, completeness, caveats, and claim text; the runtime checks provenance.",
